    "problem_statement": "Indentation Error in `pipdeptree/__init__.py`\n\nDescription\n\nAfter the recent changes, there's an indentation issue in the `pipdeptree/__init__.py` file. The error occurs when trying to execute the script, resulting in an `IndentationError: unindent does not match any outer indentation level`. This seems to be related to the `elif` statements in the `main()` function.\n\nTo reproduce the issue, you can try running the following snippet:\n\n```python\ndef main():\n    if args.json:\n        print(render_json(tree, indent=4))\n    elif args.json_tree:\n        print(render_json_tree(tree, indent=4))\n    elif args.output_format:\n        print(render_mermaid(tree))\n    elif args.output_format:\n        output = dump_graphviz(tree, output_format=args.output_format, is_reverse=args.reverse)\n```\n\nThis should trigger the indentation error, specifically pointing to the line with `elif args.json_tree:`. It seems like the indentation level is inconsistent with the rest of the function. \n\nPlease check the indentation levels in the `main()` function to ensure they are consistent."
